    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d388-a2">

                <pb facs="0914" n="818" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg818"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    999.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Ruclas to Mr.
                            Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-07-19"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 19,
                        1879</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: I have the honor to say to your
                    excellency that I have received your esteemed note dated yesterday, relative to
                    the incursions of the savage Indians on the border of Mexico and the United
                    States of America, and that I will bring its contents to the opportune knowledge
                    of the President of the republic.</p>
                <p>In support of former communications upon this subject, and of the internation of
                    the savage Indians of the United States resident in the reservation near the
                    frontier, I inclose to your excellency a copy of a telegram received to-day in
                    the department of war.</p>
                <p>I improve this opportunity to renew to your excellency the assurances of the high
                    consideration with which I am your very attentive servant.</p>
                <closer><signed>M. RUCLAS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
